--- Robfile
 1| prog: a.o b.o
 2| a.o: a.c common.h
 3| b.o: b.c common.h
 4| common.h: common.in
 5| task test: prog
$ robbie 
 robbie  ~/Robfile

 tasks
   test      ← prog

 files
 ● prog      ← a.o b.o
 ● a.o       ← a.c common.h
 ● b.o       ← b.c common.h
 ● common.h  ← common.in
exit 0
$ robbie prog test prog
done: nothing to do, in (time)
exit 0
$ robbie cc=gcc test
done: nothing to do, in (time)
exit 0
$ robbie tset
robbie: no rule makes 'tset'; did you mean 'test'?
exit 2
$ robbie nothing
robbie: no rule makes 'nothing'
exit 2
$ robbie a.c
robbie: no rule makes 'a.c'; did you mean 'a.o'?
exit 2
--- Robfile
 1| prog: main.c prog
$ robbie 
robbie: Robfile:1: 'prog' needs itself, through a loop:
robbie: Robfile:1:   prog needs prog
exit 2
--- Robfile
 1| task all: prog
 2| prog: main.o
 3| main.o: main.c gen.h
 4| 
 5| gen.h: gen.sh
 6| gen.sh: main.o
 7| task other:
$ robbie 
robbie: Robfile:3: 'main.o' needs itself, through a loop:
robbie: Robfile:3:   main.o needs gen.h
robbie: Robfile:5:   gen.h needs gen.sh
robbie: Robfile:6:   gen.sh needs main.o
exit 2
$ robbie other
robbie: Robfile:3: 'main.o' needs itself, through a loop:
robbie: Robfile:3:   main.o needs gen.h
robbie: Robfile:5:   gen.h needs gen.sh
robbie: Robfile:6:   gen.sh needs main.o
exit 2
$ robbie -p
task all: prog

prog: main.o

main.o: main.c gen.h

gen.h: gen.sh

gen.sh: main.o

task other:
exit 0
--- Robfile
 1| x: y
 2| include more.rob
--- more.rob
 1| y: x
$ robbie 
robbie: Robfile:1: 'x' needs itself, through a loop:
robbie: Robfile:1:   x needs y
robbie: more.rob:1:   y needs x
exit 2
